    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "References & Sources",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Gerhard Rühm (ed.): Die Wiener Gruppe. Achleitner Artmann Bayer Rühm Wiener. Reinbek: Rowohlt Verlag, 1967, p. 39.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Aaron Levy & Jean-Michel Rabaté (eds.): William Anastasi's Pataphysical Society: Jarry, Joyce, Duchamp and Cage. Philadelphia: Slought Books, 2005, pp. 103-105.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Stephan Beyst: \"Lawrence Weiner. And the flesh became word...\", 2002.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "\"Lawrence Weiner. And the flesh became word...\"",
          "href": "http://d-sites.net/english/weiner.htm",
          "external": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Charlie Finch: \"I AM STONED (ARE YOU STONED?)\", 2007.",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "\"I AM STONED (ARE YOU STONED?)\"",
          "href": "http://www.artnet.com/magazineus/features/finch/finch10-23-07.asp",
          "external": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Colin Lochhead: \"A conversation with Lawrence Weiner.\" Apartment Number. Toronto: A Space, 1982.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Jean-Louis Maubant: Lawrence Weiner. Specific & General Works. Nouveau Musée de Villeurbanne / Institut d'Art Contemporain, 1993.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Robert C. Morgan, \"A Conversation with Lawrence Weiner,\" Reallife 11–12 (Winter 1983).",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Maureen Mullarkey: \"Weiner's World. The reductio ad absurdum of conceptual art.\" The Weekly Standard, Vol. 13, # 6 (12/31/2007).",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "\"Weiner's World. The reductio ad absurdum of conceptual art.\"",
          "href": "http://www.weeklystandard.com/Content/Public/Articles/000/000/014/509asjhs.asp",
          "external": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Birgit Pelzer: \"Dissociated Objects: The Statements/Sculptures of Lawrence Weiner.\" October, Vol. 90 (Autumn, 1999), pp. 76-108.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Lawrence Weiner: Statements (October 12, 1969).",
      "links": [
        {
          "text": "Statements",
          "href": "http://www.ubu.com/papers/weiner_statements.html",
          "external": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Lawrence Weiner: \"Notes from Art (4 pages)\". In Clive Phillpot (ed.): Words and Word Works. Art Journal 42, no. 2 (Summer 1982).",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Concept Art & Poetry",
      "links": [],
      "level": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "\"Before he became a painter, Weiner was a poet. He no longer writes, but his book, Statements, published by Seth Siegelaub in 1968, presents his work in a form generally associated with poetry – a single phrase per page, with blank facing page, no punctuation, and such eccentric, nonhyphenated word breaks as f/rom, st/andard, pressur/e.\"",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Lucy R. Lippard: \"Art Within the Arctic Circle.\" The Hudson Review, XXII, 4 (February 1970), pp. 665-674.\n\nReprinted in: Changing. Essays in Art Criticism. New York: E.P. Dutton, 1971, pp. 277-291 [p. 286].",
      "links": []
    }
